The Serathi are avian humanoids of the western sky-roads, defined by aerial navigation, territorial memory, and high-altitude scouting culture.
Their oldest cultural claim is the first sky-reading: that landscape was first fully understood from above through memorized skyline profiles.
Before road charters named Roc Road, Serathi flight corridors already traced the same route; human trade infrastructure later followed Serathi sky geography.
Serathi law is held in roost-chronicles and corridor compacts that regulate passage, courier duty, and hunting rights across mountain and forest airspace.
They are prized as couriers and reconnaissance specialists because they can verify route truth independently of civic paperwork.
A major turning point in Serathi diplomacy was corridor formalization with lowland cities: contracted sky-road passage in exchange for recognition of Serathi territorial autonomy.
Their social code prizes direct speech, witnessed obligation, and positional honesty: claiming what you have not personally seen is treated as ethical failure.
